'''Jorge Eduardo Carinao Cárdenas''' (born 18 February 1991) is a Chilean [[Paralympic Games|paralympic]] [[Powerlifting|powerlifter]]. He is a two-time gold medalist at the [[World Para Powerlifting Championships|World Championships]] and three-time gold medalist at the [[Parapan American Games]]. He has also participated in the [[Summer Paralympic Games]] three times.

==Early life==
Of [[Mapuche]] origin, Jorge Eduardo Carinao Cárdenas was born in [[Temuco]] on 18 February 1991. The son of Carinao and Mónica Alicia Cárdenas Muñoz, he has lived most of his life in [[Padre Las Casas, Chile|Padre Las Casas]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.padrelascasas.cl/TRANSPARENCIA_MUNICIPAL/04_JULIO_2012/DECRETOS_PLC/2014/JUNIO%202014/DEC_GENERAL_MUNICIPALES/DEC%201733.pdf|website=www.padrelascasas.cl|title=Acta Concejo N44 DEL 21.02.14}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.soychile.cl/Temuco/Deportes/2015/08/08/339034/Pesista-de-Padre-Las-Casas-logro-medalla-de-oro-en-los-Parapanamericanos.aspx?fb_comment_id=929509747090109_929574810416936|website=www.soychile.cl|title=Pesista de Padre Las Casas logró el primer oro para Chile en los Parapanamericanos|date=8 August 2015|access-date=27 November 2024}}</ref>

==Career==
In December 2008, Carinao was the most promising Chilean weightlifter. At 16, he placed second at the Pan American Games in the under-17 category, while in Chile he won adult championships and broke youth records. He became paraplegic while training in weightlifting. His accident occurred after an implement fell on him.<ref name=tvn1>{{cite web|url=https://www.tvn.cl/programas/buenas-noches-a-todos/destacados/jorge-carinao-el-pesista-que-quedo-paraplejico-tras-practicar-lo-que-le|website=www.tvn.cl|title=Jorge Carinao, el pesista que quedó parapléjico tras practicar lo que le apasionaba|date=21 August 2023|access-date=23 November 2024}}</ref> At that time, Carinao turned to his family and friends for refuge, but that didn't fulfill him. Before the trauma, he dedicated himself full-time to his sport, so there was a big void to fill.<ref name=publimetro1>{{cite web|url=https://www.publimetro.cl/cl/grafico-chile/2015/08/09/historia-jorge-carinao-campeon-experto-superar-frustraciones.html|website=www.publimetro.cl|title=La historia de Jorge Carinao: Un campeón experto en superar frustraciones|date=9 August 2015|access-date=23 November 2024}}</ref> However, he didn't give up and returned to this sport.<ref name=tvn1/>

In [[2011 Parapan American Games|Guadalajara 2011]], Carabao fell in love with the sport again, although to do so he had to overcome the typical apprehensions. He went on to finished sixth.<ref name=publimetro1/> In the [[2015 Parapan American Games]], he won a gold medal. Making his Paralympic debut, he finished in sixth place at the [[2016 Summer Paralympics]].<ref name=tvn1/>

At the [[2021 World Para Powerlifting Championships|2021 World Championships]], Carinao finished in seventh place in the 65&nbsp;kg category and set a Pan American record with 190&nbsp;kg. He also won gold in the team competition.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://santiago2023.org/es/noticias/portada-sitio-web/detalle/1441/chile-dorado-jorge-carinao-oro-en-para-powerlifting-toronto-2015-es-la-medalla-que-mas-carino-le-tengo|website=santiago2023.org|title=Chile Dorado: Jorge Carinao, oro en Para powerlifting: "Toronto 2015 es la medalla que más cariño le tengo"|access-date=28 November 2024}}</ref>

In November 2023, Carinao won a gold medal for Chile in para-powerlifting at the [[2023 Parapan American Games|Parapan American Games]] held in [[Santiago]]. After this victory, he approached his girlfriend Camila Shneider to propose to her.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.biobiochile.cl/especial/parapanamericanos-santiago-2023/noticias/2023/11/20/jorge-carinao-gana-el-oro-en-para-powerlifting-y-chile-prolonga-su-jornada-dorada-en-santiago-2023.shtml |title=Jorge Carinao gana el oro en Para Powerlifting y Chile prolonga su jornada dorada en Santiago 2023 |website=Cooperativa.cl |date=20 November 2023 |access-date=20 November 2023 }}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.santiago2023.org/es/noticias/agencia-deportiva/detalle/5168/figuras-santiago-2023-jorge-carinao-oros-y-propuesta-matrimonial|website=santiago2023.org|title=Figuras Santiago 2023: Jorge Carinao, oros y propuesta matrimonial|access-date=28 November 2024}}</ref>

At the [[2025 World Para Powerlifting Championships|2025 World Championships]], Carinao won the gold medal in the 65&nbsp;kg event, in the seniors total lift.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Men's Up to 65 kg – TOTAL |url=https://www.easywl.com/cairo2025/senior/pdf/res_711_total.pdf |date=2025-10-13 |website=International Paralympic Committee |language=en}}</ref>

