'''Bruna Rafaela de Moura''' (born 24 April 1994) is a [[Brazilians|Brazilian]] [[cross-country skier]] and [[biathlete]].

She represented her country at the [[FIS Nordic World Ski Championships 2017]] in [[Lahtis]], where she finished 79th in the sprint.

Moura could not participate at the [[2022 Winter Olympics]] after suffering a heart surgery and being victim of a car accident in Austria a few days before the Olympics.<ref>{{Cite web |last=Zaccardi |first=Nick |date=23 February 2023 |title=Bruna Moura nearly died trying to get to the Olympics. Now she's back on her skis. |url=https://www.nbcsports.com/olympics/news/bruna-moura-cross-country-skiing-brazil |website=NBC Sports |access-date=22 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Reis |first=Ana Karolina |date=10 February 2026 |title=Estreante, Bruna Moura superou grave acidente para chegar à Olimpíada |trans-title=First-time athlete Bruna Moura overcame a serious accident to reach the Olympics |url=https://www.cnnbrasil.com.br/esportes/olimpiadas/estreante-bruna-moura-superou-grave-acidente-para-chegar-a-olimpiada/ |website=CNN Brasil |language=pt-BR |access-date=22 February 2026}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Riddell |first=Don |date=17 February 2026 |title=Covid, carnage and convalescence: Why one athlete's extraordinary journey to the Olympics took 16 years |url=https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/17/sport/bruna-moura-brazil-olympian |website=CNN |access-date=22 February 2026}}</ref>

==2026 Winter Olympics==
At the [[2026 Winter Olympics]] she finished in 74th place in the [[Cross-country skiing at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Women's sprint|women's sprint]] in [[Cross-country skiing at the 2026 Winter Olympics|cross-country skiing]]. In the [[Cross-country skiing at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Women's 10 kilometre freestyle|women's 10 kilometre freestyle]], she finished in 99th place.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Bruna MOURA |url=https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/results/athlete-details/39558 |work=[[Milano Cortina 2026 Olympics]] |access-date=22 February 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260223095742/https://www.olympics.com/en/milano-cortina-2026/results/athlete-details/39558 |archive-date=23 February 2026 |url-status=dead}}</ref>

Together with [[Eduarda Ribera]] she finished in 21st place in the [[Cross-country skiing at the 2026 Winter Olympics – Women's team sprint|women's team sprint]] in [[Cross-country skiing at the 2026 Winter Olympics|Cross-country skiing]] at the [[2026 Winter Olympics]], the best position by Brazilians in [[Cross-country skiing at the Winter Olympics]].

