'''Ruiter Silva''' (born 15 December 1992) is a Brazilian Paralympic swimmer and triathlete who won a silver medal in the [[Swimming at the 2016 Summer Paralympics – Men's 4 × 100 metre freestyle relay 34pts|4 × 100 metre freestyle relay]] at the [[2016 Summer Paralympics]] with [[Daniel Dias]], [[André Brasil]] and [[Phelipe Rodrigues]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Rio 2016 - swimming - mens-4x100-m-freestyle-34pts |url=https://www.paralympic.org/rio-2016/results/swimming/mens-4x100-m-freestyle-34pts |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=International Paralympic Committee |language=en}}</ref> He also competed at the [[2020 Summer Olympics]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Ruiter Silva - Swimming {{!}} Paralympic Athlete Profile |url=https://www.paralympic.org/ruiter-silva |access-date=2026-02-27 |website=International Paralympic Committee |language=en}}</ref> He has won 11 Parapan American Games medals, including 6 golds.

Silva was born with a congenital malformation in his left hand took up swimming in 2009.<ref>{{Cite news |title=Ruiter Antônio Gonçalves Silva - Comitê Paralímpico Brasileiro |url=https://cpb.org.br/atletas/ruiter-antonio-goncalves-silva/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250713022131/https://cpb.org.br/atletas/ruiter-antonio-goncalves-silva/ |archive-date=2025-07-13 |access-date=2026-02-27 |work=Comitê Paralímpico Brasileiro |language=pt-BR}}</ref>

